<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>UAH Research Dashboard</title>
  <style>
    @page {
      size: A4;
      margin: 2.6cm 2.2cm 2.4cm 2.2cm;
    }
    :root {
      --ink: #111;
      --muted: #3a3a3a;
      --line: #1f1f1f;
      --soft: #f3f3f3;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--ink);
      background: #fff;
      font-family: "Liberation Serif", "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
      font-size: 11.5pt;
      line-height: 1.42;
    }
    .doc {
      max-width: 172mm;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0;
    }
    .title-page {
      min-height: 247mm;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: space-between;
      page-break-after: always;
    }
    .title-top {
      text-align: center;
      margin-top: 18mm;
    }
    .title-top h1 {
      font-size: 20pt;
      line-height: 1.28;
      margin: 20mm 0 8mm;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .title-top h2 {
      font-size: 13pt;
      margin: 0 0 3mm;
      font-weight: 600;
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
    .title-top p {
      margin: 2mm 0;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .title-meta {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 0 auto 20mm;
      font-size: 11pt;
    }
    .title-meta td {
      padding: 2.5mm 0;
      vertical-align: top;
      border: 0;
    }
    .title-meta td:first-child {
      width: 38mm;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .small { font-size: 10.3pt; color: #222; }
    h1, h2, h3 {
      margin: 0 0 3mm;
      line-height: 1.28;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    h1 { font-size: 16.5pt; margin-top: 0; }
    h2 {
      font-size: 13pt;
      margin-top: 9mm;
      border-bottom: 0.5pt solid var(--line);
      padding-bottom: 1.5mm;
    }
    h3 {
      font-size: 11.8pt;
      margin-top: 6mm;
    }
    p { margin: 2.2mm 0; }
    ul, ol { margin: 2.5mm 0 2.5mm 6mm; padding: 0; }
    li { margin: 1.4mm 0; }
    pre {
      margin: 2.5mm 0 4mm;
      background: var(--soft);
      border: 0.6pt solid #666;
      padding: 2.6mm 2.8mm;
      overflow-x: auto;
      white-space: pre;
      font-family: "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
      font-size: 9.2pt;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }
    code {
      font-family: "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
      background: #efefef;
      padding: 0.2mm 1mm;
      border: 0.4pt solid #d7d7d7;
      border-radius: 2px;
      font-size: 10.3pt;
    }
    pre code {
      background: transparent;
      padding: 0;
      border: 0;
      font-size: inherit;
    }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 3mm 0 4mm;
      font-size: 10.8pt;
    }
    th, td {
      border: 0.6pt solid #333;
      padding: 2.2mm 2.3mm;
      vertical-align: top;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      hyphens: auto;
    }
    th {
      background: #fafafa;
      text-align: left;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .diagram {
      margin: 4mm 0 5mm;
      border: 0.6pt solid #777;
      padding: 2mm;
      background: #fff;
    }
    .diagram pre {
      margin: 0;
      border: 0;
      background: #fcfcfc;
      font-size: 10.2pt;
      white-space: pre-wrap;
    }
    .diagram svg {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
    }
    .diagram-labels {
      font-family: "Liberation Serif", "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
      font-size: 25px;
      font-weight: 700;
      fill: #111;
    }
    .lifelines {
      stroke: #999;
      stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
    }
    .messages {
      stroke: #111;
      stroke-width: 1.35;
      fill: none;
    }
    .messages text {
      stroke: none;
      fill: #111;
      font-family: "Liberation Serif", "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
      font-size: 22px;
    }
    .caption {
      margin-top: 2mm;
      font-size: 10.5pt;
      color: #222;
      font-style: italic;
      text-align: center;
    }
    blockquote {
      border: 0.6pt solid #333;
      background: #fcfcfc;
      margin: 3mm 0;
      padding: 2.6mm 3mm;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    a { color: #111; }
  </style>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/harness-theme.css" />
<script defer src="../assets/harness-theme.js"></script>
<style>
.doc code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.research-controls { margin: 1rem 0; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 18px; background: var(--card); }
.research-controls button, .research-controls input, .research-controls select {
  color: var(--ink); background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 8px; padding: .55rem .7rem; margin: .2rem; font: inherit; }
.research-controls button { cursor: pointer; }
.research-controls button[aria-pressed="true"] { background: var(--blue); color: white; }
.research-controls label { display: inline-block; margin-top: .7rem; }
@media print { .research-controls { display: none; } [hidden] { display: table-row; } }
</style></head>
<body>
  <main class="doc">

<h1>UAH Research Dashboard</h1>
<p>Reconciled: 2026-10-08. Scope: research metadata and source navigation. <a href="uah_research_dashboard.html">HTML view</a>, <a href="experiment_registry.json">registry</a>, <a href="../artifacts/research/README.md">artifact catalog</a>.</p>
<h2>Authority and recorded boundaries</h2>
<p>The <a href="../plans/universal_agentic_harness_masterplan.md">canonical masterplan</a> owns release order and gates. <a href="../architecture/neural_workbench_adaptive_ab_harness.md">NeuralWorkbench architecture</a> owns the adaptive research boundary. Dated investigations and reviews support specific claims about their inspected bytes. This index is neither a second roadmap nor an Observatory O1 runtime view.</p>
<p>The September Jev note proposes closed-candidate ranking. No executed UAH Jev experiment is recorded here. H1 context persistence is an implementation dependency named by the masterplan, distinct from H3 candidate context/retrieval and H4 quarantined crystallization research. This catalog defines no context tree, evidence-freshness rule or AB mapping.</p>
<p>The R0 receipt records executed diagnostics. The R1 review receipts concern a compiler-only domain-pack identity repair, not all H0/H1 consumers or H2 parity. Their observed values, original finding IDs and reviewed-byte identities remain in the linked receipts. Live provider transport, model quality, owner-proven effects and release qualification are separate evidence claims.</p>
<h2>Catalog</h2>
<p>Record kinds describe document content, not a promotion ladder. A proposal does not become an executed probe merely because it contains a test design. An executed probe may be unsuccessful; a reviewed outcome may reject a change. H-series dependencies are links, not declarations that prerequisites passed. Scoring is <code>not_scored</code> in this metadata view; consult source receipts for their actual observations. No direct comparability is inferred from labels or AB depth.</p>
