<h3>Configuration-level evaluation investigation</h3>
<p>Literature and runtime trade-off investigation. No controlled UAH model or adaptive-uplift experiment is established by this note.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>evaluation-investigation</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>b729cbf7f24dd3d28f0c871c4e0333d11c2face06a313d2a63c8097d4fa2afe4</code>.</p>
<h3>Jev and System One investigation</h3>
<p>Primary-source investigation of closed typed decisions and local substitutes. Vendor claims and capacity estimates are not UAH measurements.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>jev-investigation</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>27b76bcf3c34604e204c5c347ff5de4ec8b6827f317fbf641290c7bb362183da</code>.</p>
<h3>Jev closed-candidate ranking proposal</h3>
<p>The September note proposes deterministic controls and shadow ranking after H0/H1 closure. No executed Jev experiment, access qualification or calibrated UAH result is recorded.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>jev-ranking-proposal</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>27b76bcf3c34604e204c5c347ff5de4ec8b6827f317fbf641290c7bb362183da</code>.</p>
<p>Reference: <a href="../architecture/neural_workbench_adaptive_ab_harness.md">Open document</a>.</p>
<h3>R0 exit contracts and provider routes</h3>
<p>Research handoff on exit-contract alternatives and provider routes. Route availability is not execution authority or owner evidence; live qualification remains unscored.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>r0-exit-investigation</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>3d7d94e38df060428cb2d6a643bf5da3bba699a3c4e4be3e3361706b93545975</code>.</p>
<h3>R1 effect evidence and trace contract alternatives</h3>
<p>Research alternatives for proof meaning, temporal validity and trace representation. The proposed train/holdout fixtures were not executed; no new freshness policy was accepted.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>r1-evidence-investigation</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>bf5549f3eb3f53efaeb2d9d5c10d6b70f39373131c5b47e9b4a386a4d2548aa5</code>.</p>
<h3>R0 saved counterexample diagnostics</h3>
<p>Completed local diagnostics are recorded in the dated receipt. A zero diagnostic exit does not imply a passing conformance gate, live model quality or release closure.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>r0-recorded-probes</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>90d99f7e21e6d67e1cef0cadd7c3bef5782fb13546192c7870e683a6d0dbf507</code>.</p>
<h3>R1 compiler-only domain-pack repair receipt</h3>
<p>The receipt records replacement and nested-tamper compiler regressions, an unchanged valid control and scoped review links. It does not close other mechanisms or all H0/H1 deliverables.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>r1-compiler-repair</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>4408dadc970e75fe2f94d0bdd63478c4e9b9aab0074164c86682a000adf959e8</code>.</p>
<p>Reference: <a href="../artifacts/reviews/2026-10-08_uah_r1_domain_pack_primary_review.md">Open document</a>.</p>
<p>Reference: <a href="../artifacts/reviews/2026-10-08_uah_r1_domain_pack_second_review.md">Open document</a>.</p>
<h3>R1 compiler-only primary review</h3>
<p>Historical APPROVE receipt for the named three-file compiler repair against exact frozen-before bytes. Reviewed runtime hashes inside the source define its scope, not the current checkout.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>r1-primary-review</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>14da7145ad7a3b3f575d4438a5d959abdbd7923c65655be788ae19f52eb8abab</code>.</p>
<h3>R1 compiler-only second review</h3>
<p>Historical distinct-model APPROVE receipt with a representation-only limitation outside the repair. This source snapshot hash identifies the stored document, not a fresh certification of runtime changes.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>r1-second-review</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>85a97f05f2ec16668acf7fc310277558908820bcd98d780416fc7ea469c6b284</code>.</p>
<h3>H1 runtime and context-persistence dependency</h3>
<p>Consult the current masterplan H1 section for runtime/context deliverables and open evidence. This unpinned link supplies no release status or context-tree schema.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>h1-context-dependency</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>unpinned dependency link</code>.</p>
<h3>H3 trace-adaptive search dependency</h3>
<p>Consult the masterplan and architecture for candidate-only search, retrieval and context. These are dependencies, not adopted experiments or a second roadmap.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>h3-search-dependency</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>unpinned dependency link</code>.</p>
<p>Reference: <a href="../architecture/neural_workbench_adaptive_ab_harness.md">Open document</a>.</p>
<h3>H4 quarantined crystallization dependency</h3>
<p>Consult the canonical H4 gate for reviewed promotion and rollback. Frequency or display labels cannot promote research artifacts or transfer environment-owner authority.</p>
<p>Catalog ID: <code>h4-crystallization-dependency</code>. Source snapshot SHA-256: <code>unpinned dependency link</code>.</p>
<p>Reference: <a href="../architecture/neural_workbench_adaptive_ab_harness.md">Open document</a>.</p>
<h2>Using the sources</h2>
<p>Consult the source before interpreting a catalog label. A source snapshot hash identifies the indexed document bytes; it does not revalidate runtime provenance or retrospectively approve other changes. Reference links are navigation only. Update metadata only after the source document is complete, retain historical evidence and regenerate both files. <a href="README.md">Catalog rules</a> describe the bounded update procedure.</p>
  </main>
<script>
(() => {
  const table = [...document.querySelectorAll('table')].find(
    item => item.querySelector('th')?.textContent === 'Research record');
  if (!table) return;
  const controls = document.getElementById('research-tabs');
  const search = document.getElementById('research-search');
  const gate = document.getElementById('research-gate');
  const count = document.getElementById('research-count');
  const rows = [...table.querySelectorAll('tbody tr')];
  let selected = 'all';
  function apply() {
    const query = search.value.trim().toLowerCase();
    let visible = 0;
    rows.forEach(row => {
      const cells = row.querySelectorAll('td');
      const kind = cells[1].textContent.trim();
      const dependencies = cells[3].textContent.split(',').map(item => item.trim());
      const matches = (selected === 'all' || kind === selected)
        && (gate.value === 'all' || dependencies.includes(gate.value))
        && row.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(query);
      row.hidden = !matches;
      if (matches) visible += 1;
    });
    count.textContent = visible ? `${visible} catalog records` : 'No matching catalog records.';
  }
  controls.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(button => {
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      selected = button.dataset.kind;
      controls.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(other =>
        other.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(other === button)));
      apply();
    });
  });
  search.addEventListener('input', apply);
  gate.addEventListener('change', apply);
  apply();
})();
</script></body>
</html>
